<%#
  THE PAGE INTRO, IN EDIT MODE (2026-09-09, content blocks; spec §3). The cover and the description
  are the two things above the grid that a maker could not change from this page, and they are
  drafted here like everything else: layout_editor_controller.js reads `data-cover` and
  `data-description` off this card into the draft's `page` mapping, and the ONE Save writes them
  beside the layout. Outside edit mode nothing changes — the description paragraph and
  projects/_hero render exactly as they did.

  THE PICKER LISTS THE FOLDER'S IMAGES AND NOTHING ELSE (spec decision 4), the same set an image
  block picks from: the YAML names a picture by its path UNDER the project folder, and a file
  elsewhere in the library has no such path. A cover set from a file's own page from outside the
  folder KEEPS WORKING — it is a raw column and this card never clears it — the picker simply
  cannot choose one, and the export says so rather than dropping it silently
  (Maker::LayoutDocument::COVER_OUTSIDE_NOTE).

  Reads @project, @page_nodes (for the cover's own name — a tombstoned cover has none, and "No
  cover" is the honest word for a picture that is not there), @folder_images and @page_thumbs.
%>
<% cover_id = @project.cover_node_id %>
<% cover_node = cover_id && @page_nodes[cover_id] %>
<div class="page-intro panel" data-layout-editor-target="page"
     data-cover="<%= cover_id %>" data-description="<%= @project.description %>">
  <div class="page-intro-cover">
    <b>Cover</b>
    <div class="cover-current" data-layout-editor-target="coverName"><%= cover_node ? cover_node.name : "No cover" %></div>
    <div class="image-picker" role="group" aria-label="Pick a cover from the project folder">
      <% if @folder_images.empty? %>
        <p class="muted">No images in the project folder yet.</p>
      <% end %>
      <% @folder_images.each do |row| %>
        <% ext = File.extname(row.node.name).delete(".").upcase.first(4) %>
        <button type="button" class="cover-pick image-pick<%= " active" if cover_id == row.node_id %>"
                data-node-id="<%= row.node_id %>" data-action="layout-editor#pickCover" title="<%= row.node.name %>">
          <%= render "files/thumb", thumb: @page_thumbs.thumb(row.node_id), ext_label: ext,
                     url: preview_src(@page_thumbs.thumb(row.node_id)) %>
          <span class="image-pick-name"><%= row.node.name %></span>
        </button>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <button type="button" class="linkbtn small" data-action="layout-editor#removeCover">Remove cover</button>
  </div>
  <%# PLAIN TEXT, AND ITS LINE BREAKS ARE CONTENT: Maker::LayoutDocument strips the description but
      never collapses it, and the page renders it as the column holds it. %>
  <label class="field page-intro-description"><span>Description</span>
    <textarea rows="4" data-action="input->layout-editor#description"><%= @project.description %></textarea></label>
</div>
